        "original_id": "83ccbc5d-a37a-5fa7-97b1-d51ce304db34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph-Armand Bombardier\n- Companies: Bombardier Inc.\n- Places: Bombardier Glacier, Montreal, Quebec, Canada\n- Organizations: Falkland Islands Dependencies Survey, UK Antarctic Place-Names Committee\n- Products: snowmobile\n- Topics: aerospace, transportation\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph-Armand Bombardier was born on April 16, 1907, and died on February 18, 1964.\n- From 1926 to 1937, Joseph-Armand Bombardier developed the snowmobile as one of the earliest successful self-propelled over-snow vehicles.\n- Joseph-Armand Bombardier was a French-Canadian inventor and businessman.\n- Joseph-Armand Bombardier founded Bombardier Inc.\n- Joseph-Armand Bombardier's most famous invention was the snowmobile.\n- In 1960 and 1961, the Falkland Islands Dependencies Survey mapped Bombardier Glacier.\n- The UK Antarctic Place-Names Committee named Bombardier Glacier for Joseph-Armand Bombardier.\n- Bombardier Inc. is a multinational aerospace and transportation company based in Montreal, Quebec, Canada.",
